{"NoopCache used for in-proc AuthZ client disables client-side caching, defeating caching benefits and potentially causing higher DB load and latency for repeated checks in high-traffic environments": 0.46972739696502686, "Potential data race when reading permission cache maps - the code stores per-user permissions as map[string]bool and returns that map directly to callers, which can cause race conditions if another goroutine updates the same cache entry concurrently": 0.18700700998306274, "Denial cache needs comprehensive test coverage for all code paths: denial cache hit short-circuits, denial cache TTL semantics, and scenario where denial cache misses but permission is later denied": 0.08235197514295578, "getUserPermissions uses singleflight.Do and returns res.(map[string]bool) type assertion which could panic if Do returns nil or different type due to unexpected path": 0.13637284934520721, "Tests rely on internal cache semantics and need additional coverage for edge cases like concurrent cache refresh, cache eviction boundaries, and cross-identity-type caching coherency": 0.009798702783882618, "Hard to audit token-exchange / in-proc server interaction with potential for token leakage if in-proc interceptor is misconfigured": 0.0019649167079478502, "CHANGELOG.md not updated to describe new authz caching features (NoopCache, denial cache, getCachedIdentityPermissions, shadow-proxy)": 0.009224510751664639, "High commit churn with multiple merge commits raises risk of subtle regressions and conflicts in RBAC/cache paths": 0.0023734504356980324, "No explicit CONTRIBUTING.md file observed - should confirm it covers new authz caching changes and testing guidelines": 0.04888559505343437}